  },
  {
   "lever": "precomputed / incremental key norms (maintain nk across tokens instead of recomputing the tile)",
   "verdict": "not worth a bracket + the incremental form is not bit-identical",
   "reason": "only one slot's key changes per token, so recomputing only the hit slot's norm is value-identical, but the recompute is <= 2*R*K of ~194K ops per token-row (~2%): bounded below relevance; the arithmetic incremental update (sum += new - old) is not the defined recompute and is not bit-identical"
  },
